WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Find the cabinet in your drawing. The highlighted label identifies the cabinet. Keep the drawing page with it so you can check the original.

2
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:16.000
Keep the code and its source. The code connects this cabinet to its drawing. Confirm the quantity to order from the drawing and installation site.

3
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Choose the matching cabinet. Compare the two catalog options: B3000 has one upper drawer; B3100 has two. The doors and shelf stay the same.

4
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:32.000
See how the cabinet opens. Open the drawers and doors, then look at the shelf inside. Compare the storage before choosing a cabinet.

5
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Check the cabinet dimensions. Compare the catalog size with the space in your room. Confirm measurements, quantity, finish and price before ordering.

6
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:48.000
See the cabinet in warm oak. This room preview shows a 36-inch oak cabinet. Explore the look before planning the room around it.

7
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:56.000
Fit it between the other cabinets. The cabinet lines up with its neighbours and slides beneath the shared worktop. The opening must be wide enough.

8
00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:04.000
See the whole room come together. Explore the fitted cabinet, worktable, seating and garden view. Keep the drawing, fit notes and item list for your next step.
